actress Ella Blair's revelation that she  has multiple sclerosis is being met by  an outpouring of support the 46 year old  star disclosed her diagnosis and an  emotional Instagram post it was liked by  nearly 90,000 people she writes I am  disabled I fall sometimes I drop things  my memory is foggy and my left side is  asking for directions from a broken GPS  the post is bringing new attention to  multiple sclerosis and dr. Tara Narula  is here with the symptoms and the  treatments Tara good morning good  morning bianna multiple sclerosis or MS  is a nervous system disease that can  cause pain and numbness to loss of  vision and motor functions nearly 1  million people in the u.s. live with a  disease there's no cure but treatment  can help manage symptoms and slow its  progression you almost had me fooled  actress selma Blair most famous for her  roles in films like Legally Blonde and  cruel intentions I do like it I think  all the time is back on set for a new  project and facing a new challenge  Blair posted this selfie Saturday  revealing she was diagnosed with  multiple sclerosis back in August she  writes I am in the thick of it but I  hope to give some hope to others and  even to myself  neurologist dr. Fred Lublin we know that  it's an abnormality of the immune system  but we don't know what sets it off in  those affected by MS the body's immune  system eats away at the protective  covering of nerves disrupting  communication between the brain and the  body studies suggest the risk of  developing the disease is increased by  both genetic and environmental factors  including smoking low vitamin D and  adolescent obesity ms affects women  about three times as often as men and  that ratio actually has been going up  there are hormonal possibilities that  are being investigated but not yet  entirely clear why that difference  exists what do we have to talk about  Blair is in her mid-40s researchers say  most people are diagnosed between ages  20 and 50 with a wide range of symptoms  there are some people who may go through  their entire lives and never knows they  have MS and then there's some people who  can have very severe disability from the  disease and everything in between other  public figures with MS include Ann  Romney Jack Osbourne and Montel Williams  we have 15 different treatments that are  on the market at present that alter the  course of the illness we have lots and  lots of individuals who lead normal  productive lives as Blair writes I want  to play with my son again I want to walk  down the street and ride my horse I have  MS and I am okay  Blair plans to continue her work  starring in the upcoming Netflix series  another life by putting yet another  public face on Ms Blair could help  others to recognize potential symptoms  and meet with their doctor so great to  know that the son was continuing with  her work as well what are the symptoms  that people should be looking for Terra  there can be a lot of different symptoms  ranging from fatigue to loss of vision  or double vision loss of bowel or  bladder function  a sensation of numbness or tingling in  the face arms or legs muscle spasticity  so it can be very difficult sometimes to  pick up the diagnosis because people can  have these different symptoms that can  happen over years Thank You dr. Tara  thank you
 

